author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "pm graph impact applies a default row bound consistent with its sibling subcommands, and the bound is declared in contract data rather than hardcoded per subcommand; Truncated results disclose has_more and a resumable cursor so no reachable node becomes unreachable through the default; A test asserts default-invocation output size for every graph subcommand against a real-scale fixture, so a future subcommand cannot ship unbounded; Unbounded traversal remains available through an explicit flag and is documented; The help text's 'bounded' claim is true of every subcommand it covers, asserted structurally"
goal: project management = context management
objective: "A command group that declares bounded semantics must honour them on every member, especially the member agents are routed to"
value: Removes a 57k-token default from the traversal agents are told to use for semantic reachability
impact: Makes typed-graph reachability answerable inside an agent's context budget instead of consuming a quarter of it
